# Patch1 and patch2 start from versions of f with different lines between
# prefix19 and suffix00. Patch1 removes its three, backport_removed0 to
# backport_removed2. Patch2 removes its four, upstream_removed0 to
# upstream_removed3, and adds new_upstream_result in their place. The report
# must show the two blocks of removals side by side and new_upstream_result on
# patch2's side. The source and result files hold f before and after each patch,
# and the runner checks that each patch turns its source into its result with no
# fuzz.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: patch1 patch2
